# Directories that must never be traversed as Bazel packages.
#
# IMPORTANT: this file is parsed by Gazelle as well as Bazel, and Gazelle
# rejects glob patterns outright:
#     gazelle: the .bazelignore exclusion pattern must not be a glob bazel-*
# Every pattern below is therefore a literal. The globs that were here before
# (`bazel-*`, `*.swp`, `*.swo`, `*~`, `*.tmp`, `*.log`, `*.profraw`, `*.pyc`,
# `*.pyo`, `*.pyd`, `*.local.bazelrc`) are valid for Bazel but produced eleven
# errors on every `bazel run //:gazelle` - enough noise to bury a real failure.
# None of them were load-bearing:
#
#   * Bazel already refuses to traverse its own convenience symlinks
#     (bazel-out, bazel-bin, bazel-testlogs, bazel-<workspace>), so listing them
#     explicitly is belt-and-braces. They are still listed, by name, because the
#     literal form is the only one both tools accept.
#   * The rest are single-file artefacts (editor swaps, logs, bytecode). A file
#     with no BUILD file in its directory cannot become a Bazel package, so
#     ignoring them buys nothing.
#
# If you need a new exclusion, add the literal path. Do not add a glob.
bazel-bin
bazel-out
bazel-testlogs
bazel-ecommerce

# Version control and editor state.
.git
.gitignore
.idea
.vscode

# OS metadata.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Build and packaging output.
dist
out
tmp
temp

# Test and profiling output.
test-results
coverage
logs

# Third-party dependency trees.
node_modules
vendor
__pycache__

# Local Bazel state.
.bazel
user.bazelrc
local.bazelrc

# Generated documentation.
docs/_build
site
